# Project context

Canonical project docs live in `.context/`. Read the relevant module before making changes; do not copy those docs into other rule files.

- @.context/overview.md — stack, goals, mobile-first philosophy
- @.context/architecture.md — layout, routing, navigation shell
- @.context/ui-guidelines.md — Beer CSS, icons, theming, touch targets
- @.context/conventions.md — pnpm, TypeScript, git

## Operational defaults

1. Use `pnpm` only (`pnpm install`, `pnpm add`, `pnpm dev`, `pnpm build`).
2. Style with Beer CSS semantic HTML and utility classes. Do not add another UI library unless asked.
3. Icons are Material Symbols via `<i>icon_name</i>`.
4. Keep tap targets at least 48px and respect mobile safe areas.
5. Do not create git commits unless the user explicitly asks.
